[
    {
        "content": "<p>If I've written a macro that expands to a command, how can I see what the macro expands to?  This is essential for debugging, but I don't see any easy way to do it.</p>\n<p>For example, consider this simple macro:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"foo\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"bar\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">-- expands to \"def z := 3\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- prints 3</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>For debugging purposes, I'd like to see the command that <code>foo z bar 3</code> expands to.  The best I've come up with is to edit the macro definition to look like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"foo\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"bar\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">dbg_trace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Then <code>foo z bar 3</code> prints</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Command</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">declaration</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Command</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">declModifiers</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[])</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Command</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">definition</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"s2\">\"def\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Command</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">declId</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[])</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Command</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">optDeclSig</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[])</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Command</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">declValSimple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\":=\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"3\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Termination</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">suffix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[])</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[])</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[]))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This is not easy to read (especially for larger macros).  I want to see just the expansion <code>def z := 3</code>.</p>\n<p>There is a function that will pretty-print a command:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">PrettyPrinter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ppCommand</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Command</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CoreM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Format</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Presumably this would give me the command in a nicer format.  But it runs in the <code>CoreM</code> monad, which is not available to me in the macro expansion where we are in <code>MacroM</code>.  So I can't see any way to call it.</p>\n<p>Does anyone have any advice?</p>",
        "id": 614851964,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1785962989
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>you can use <code>#infotrees in</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"foo\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"bar\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">num</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  • [MacroExpansion]</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    foo z bar 3 -- expands to \"def z := 3\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">    ===&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    def z :=</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">      3 -- expands to \"def z := 3\"</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">substring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">info_trees</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">-- expands to \"def z := 3\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- prints 3</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 614854211,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1785963899
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Extremely useful!  Thanks!</p>\n<p>Meanwhile, I've realized that <code>set_option trace.Elab.info true</code> will print much the same information.</p>\n<p>By the way, I don't see <code>#info_trees</code> mentioned in the language reference anywhere (except in the release notes for 4.18.0 last year).</p>",
        "id": 614858215,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1785965846
    }
]